"""
sample_titles.py - the hand-written title list behind the bundled DEMO dataset.

make_sample_data.py reads these lines and turns them into MovieLens-style files plus a
"pre-fetched metadata" file, so the whole pipeline can run with no internet and no API keys.

IMPORTANT - this is DEMO data:
  * titles, years, directors, cast, runtimes, languages and certificates are real (written from
    general knowledge, so small mistakes are possible);
  * every overview is an ORIGINAL one-line summary written for this project (not copied from
    TMDB, IMDb or Wikipedia);
  * imdb_rating / metascore / popularity are plausible values, not live numbers;
  * tmdb / imdb ids are filled only where we are confident, otherwise left empty;
  * ml_id is the real MovieLens movieId when known, otherwise empty (the generator then gives the
    title a demo id >= 900001 that can never clash with a real MovieLens id).

Line format (fields separated by ';', lists separated by '|'):
  MOVIES: ml_id;title;year;genres;directors;cast;runtime;lang;cert;keywords;collection;tmdb;imdb;
          imdb_rating;metascore;pop;overview
  SERIES: tmdb;title;first_year;genres;creators;cast;episode_runtime;seasons;lang;cert;keywords;
          imdb;imdb_rating;pop;overview
  pop = rough popularity tier from 1 (niche) to 10 (blockbuster).
"""

